WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.107
Five nodes, each pointing at the next.

00:04.107 --> 00:14.700
You could copy the values into a new, backwards list, but that costs a new node for every old one.

00:15.000 --> 00:26.602
Instead, walk the list with two pointers: prev behind, curr ahead.

00:26.602 --> 00:31.700
Nothing moves but the arrows.

00:32.000 --> 00:42.641
For each node, save next first, then point curr back at prev.

00:42.641 --> 00:47.700
Never cut before you hold on.

00:48.000 --> 00:55.856
One pass, O(n) time, and not a single new node.

00:55.856 --> 00:59.700
That’s the linked list.
